+For $k=d+1$ give $W$ its expected zero-dimensional structure; for $k>d+1$
+use the empty zero-dimensional structure without an expected-dimension
+claim. All product-end equations and framing restrictions are equalities
+of empty maps, so [F4] gives the required framed cobordism directly.
+For the remainder assume $k\le d$. [F3, F4, given, cases, construct]
 
